//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 60 - THE CHAMPION'S SHORT MIRROR, MEASURED HONESTLY FOR THE FIRST TIME IN THIS LAB.
//
// THE STORED PROMPT describes a board state (Attack 37, "earned a filter stack") that is now more
// than twenty attacks stale -- Attack 41 closed Attack 37, Attack 43 closed the sweep-reversal family,
// Attack 46 is the champion (level-target tap-and-hold, RR floor 3.5, both halves clear, cold-
// reproduced), and Attack 47 exhausted its filter stack on the ~77% sample wall (HARD LESSON 49).
// Attacks 48-59 (twelve straight new-mechanism-or-refinement proposals) all failed on H1, three of them
// (50, 51, 59) on the SAME inverted-payoff shape: majority win rate, average loser bigger than average
// winner. THE DOCS OVERRIDE THE PROMPT, per the prompt's own instruction.
//
// ==================== WHAT THIS CYCLE ACTUALLY DOES, AND WHY IT IS NOT A THIRTEENTH GUESS ====================
// Every discovery attempt in this lab has been LONG ONLY. The STANDING REQUIREMENT (user directive,
// 2026-09-02) demands both directions, built separately, with the short's own geometry -- never a
// sign-flipped mirror -- but the CORRECTED no-mirror rule (2026-09-02) says: BUILD THE MIRROR FIRST,
// THEN FIX LOCATION. A symmetric construction is a legitimate starting point, not a banned shortcut.
// This lab has never run that first step, because HARD LESSON 42/43 (War Formation E64a/E71, 3M v57/v60,
// 2026-09-04) established something this lab's own CHAMPION-BOARD already recorded as a wall
// (line ~2652, pre-E71): at 100%-of-equity sizing, a SHORT position's required margin RISES as the
// trade moves against it while equity FALLS, so the two cross almost immediately and the engine
// force-closes the position at ~0.01%-0.6% adverse -- long before any real stop can fire. A LONG's
// margin requirement shrinks with an adverse move, so longs never hit this wall; every long result in
// this lab (Attacks 1-59) is genuine. Every SHORT this lab has never even tried would have hit it.
// THE FIX, proven twice already (War Formation E71: PF 0.454->0.973; 3M v57->v60: PF 1.223->1.886,
// win rate 25.6%->56.4%): cut position size to 25% of equity via an EXPLICIT Pine `qty=` on
// strategy.entry, because the parity profile force-overrides `default_qty_value` back to 100 -- the
// qty argument is the only channel that survives. This is a DECLARED DEVIATION, labelled here and in
// every record of this run, and NOT comparable to Attack 46's 100%-equity long numbers on return or
// drawdown (both scale with position fraction). Profit factor, win rate, achieved ratio and trade count
// ARE comparable -- they are ratios of a uniform per-trade scalar, the same leverage-invariance argument
// the LEVERAGE section of this ledger already applies to leverage itself.
//
// THE MIRROR ITSELF is Attack 46 byte-for-byte, flipped: resistance tapped and held (a level-target
// SHORT, not a sign-flip of the long's economics) instead of support tapped and held, target the
// LOWER level instead of the higher one, stop beyond the tap bar's own high instead of its own low.
// Same lookback (20), same tap tolerance (0.10%), same RR floor (3.5), same R floor (0.8% by
// exclusion), same max hold (192 bars). Nothing about the SIGNAL logic changed -- only direction and
// the declared sizing deviation this direction requires to be measurable at all.
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg (SHORT ONLY -- this is the leg the standing requirement has never gotten):
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - enforced by EXCLUSION via rBig on rShort = high - close, never clamped.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = the tap bar's own high, the actual extreme of the test
//        of resistance. Not an ATR, not a percentage, not the signal price.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6, scoped by HARD LESSON 31) - SHORT ONLY. Not blended with Attack 46's
//        long. The mirror is the DECLARED starting point per the corrected no-mirror rule, not a claim
//        that location is already right -- if this fails, the next move is fixing location, not another
//        sizing tweak.
//   BINDING (E17) - the RR floor NECESSARILY binds, since it rejects setups outright; trade count is
//        read before anything else, same as Attack 44-46.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) - minRpct (absolute stop distance) and minRRv (reward geometry) are independent;
//        a wide stop can pass one and fail the other.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - sup/res are both [1]-shifted, strictly prior bars; the tap and the
//        hold are read on the current bar and entry fires at its close -- identical construction to
//        Attack 44-46's proven-safe same-bar candle read, not a coil+thrust same-bar contradiction.
//   OCCUPANCY (LESSONS 24/28/29) - pyramiding=1, an open position blocks later entries; named in
//        advance because a level target produces variable hold times by construction.
//   CASCADE / MARGIN ARTIFACT (HARD LESSON 42/43) - the reason this build exists. VERIFY with
//        get_trades before trusting the result: losers must exit at CONSISTENT distances near the tap
//        bar's own high, not at scattered tiny adverse distances. A scattered pattern means 25% was
//        still not enough and the result is not yet trustworthy.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17):
//   * H1 PF >= 1.0 AND loss distances consistent (margin artifact absent) -> the first honestly
//     measured short edge in this lab's history; run H2, per the mandate's kill-rule structure.
//   * H1 PF < 1.0 -> DISCARDED by the kill rule. No filters, no rescue, no H2, regardless of credit
//     balance -- the mandate's explicit instruction. The declared-deviation fix will still be recorded
//     as validated (or not) via the loss-distance check, separate from the mechanism's own verdict.
//   * MAJORITY WIN RATE but achieved ratio well below the 3.5 floor's promise -> the inverted-payoff
//     shape (Attacks 50, 51, 59) recurring a fourth time, now on the short side -- report win rate
//     alongside achieved ratio explicitly, per the board's own standing risk note.
//   * FEWER THAN ~30 TRADES -> a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12).
//   * LOSS DISTANCES SCATTERED AND SUB-0.8% -> 25% equity was insufficient; the margin ceiling is not
//     fully cleared and the result is NOT a measurement of the mechanism, per HARD LESSON 42/43's own
//     warning about trusting a win rate before checking this.
strategy("BTC Attack60 level target SHORT mirror 25pct equity", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

lookback = input.int(20,     "Level lookback, bars -- sets BOTH the resistance tapped and the low targeted")
tapTol   = input.float(0.10, "Tap tolerance, % -- how close to resistance counts as a tap")
minRRv   = input.float(3.5,  "Minimum reward:risk the GEOMETRY must offer, else skip -- mirrors Attack 46")
minRpct  = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
maxBars  = input.int(192,    "Max bars in trade")
eqFrac   = input.float(0.25, "DECLARED DEVIATION: fraction of equity per position -- HARD LESSON 42/43")

sup = ta.lowest(low,   lookback)[1]
res = ta.highest(high, lookback)[1]

tapped  = not na(res) and high  >= res * (1 - tapTol / 100)
held    = not na(res) and close < res
setupOn = tapped and held

rShort = high - close
reward = na(sup) ? na : close - sup
minR   = close * minRpct / 100
rBig   = rShort >= minR
rrOk   = not na(reward) and rShort > 0 and reward / rShort >= minRRv

goShort = setupOn and rBig and rrOk

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat   = strategy.position_size == 0
qtyUse = strategy.equity * eqFrac / close

if flat and goShort and qtyUse > 0
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty = qtyUse)
    slPx   := high
    tpPx   := sup
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("SX", from_entry="S", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goShort ? 1 : 0, title="ShortSignal")
plot(res, title="Resistance")
plot(sup, title="TargetLevel")
